  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of a crowd of figures with ringed helmet heads standing in a street between buildings, looking up at a sky of pink and yellow stripes.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. Eight or nine figures with round helmeted heads ringed in mint, pink and blue, their faces a few hash strokes, stand close together in the lower half, dressed in blue, orange, red and olive coats. Behind them a street of brown and olive buildings with window slots recedes toward a central vanishing point. Above the street, radiating stripes of pink, yellow and blue fan out from the horizon like a sunrise or a stage curtain, with green smoke shapes drifting across. Two small screens with squiggles hang on the buildings. Thick black outlines and visible brushwork.",
    "impression": "The crowd has stopped in the street to watch something happen in the sky, and the viewer stands among them. The fanned stripes could be dawn, an aurora, or a signal. It is the most cinematic Superland painting: a moment of shared attention.",
